WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:01.950
The guy who directed "Underworld?"

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:03.250
A new writer, too?

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:07.689
Is the draw of Ana de Armas enough to bring
in dedicated "John Wick" fans, or will the

00:00:07.689 --> 00:00:08.950
spinoff flop?

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.610
Here's why fans are worried.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:15.570
When John Wick first arrived in theaters back
in 2014, the Keanu Reeves vehicle turned out

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.040
to be a breath of fresh air in a sea of middling
action thrillers.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.800
The simple-but-effective revenge plot is emotionally
compelling enough that it allows audiences

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.300
to get behind Wick as he slaughters mobsters
with varying degrees of brutality.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.899
Combined with killer direction from notable
stunt coordinators Chad Stahelski and David

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.829
Leitch, it's a rollicking movie that packs
a genuine punch.

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:38.800
"Yeah, I'm thinking I'm back."

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.350
From there, the franchise flourished as John
Wick: Chapter 2 arrived in 2017, and John

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.960
Wick: Chapter 3 — Parabellum swiftly followed
in 2019.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:53.210
The third film raked in just over $327 million
worldwide, so it's unsurprising that Lionsgate

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:57.820
quickly gave Stahelski the greenlight to work
on John Wick: Chapter 4, which is set for

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:58.929
release in 2023.

00:00:58.929 --> 00:01:03.929
And, of course, there are also a few other
John Wick projects in the pipeline, including

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:09.180
a TV show revolving around the Continental
Hotel, and a spin-off movie known as Ballerina.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.640
The feature film will follow one of the ballerina
assassins who briefly show up in Parabellum,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.450
and it's set to star Knives Out and No Time
To Die alum Ana de Armas in the lead role.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:22.649
Lionsgate recently confirmed that the movie
is supposed to start filming later this year,

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.740
but John Wick fans are already worried about
the spin-off.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.539
Of course, the news that Ballerina is set
to start filming later this year obviously

00:01:29.539 --> 00:01:34.210
has some fans excited about diving back into
the John Wick universe, but others are concerned

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.970
about who's attached to the project.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:40.119
The film is directed by Len Wiseman, who's
best known for helming two of the Underworld

00:01:40.119 --> 00:01:44.840
movies, as well as Live Free or Die Hard and
the 2012 remake of Total Recall.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:49.180
The middling quality of these movies has fans
skeptical about what's ahead in the next chapter

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:50.340
of the Wickverse.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.240
As one Reddit user recently posted:

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.979
"I like Underworld but those movies got worse
and worse [...] These guys on the same project

00:01:56.979 --> 00:01:59.179
screams mindless action movie."

00:01:59.179 --> 00:02:03.399
Meanwhile, another user voiced their concerns
about the involvement of John Wick: Chapter

00:02:03.399 --> 00:02:05.999
3 and Army of the Dead writer Shay Hatten.

00:02:05.999 --> 00:02:06.999
They said:

00:02:06.999 --> 00:02:09.700
"Hatten and Wiseman films are not typically
films I get hyped about.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.959
I liked John Wick 3, so if the fourth one
is solid Hatten may have found his niche.

00:02:13.959 --> 00:02:17.190
But Hatten in combination with Wiseman gets
me worried."

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:21.359
However, it's entirely possible Wiseman has
changed his directing style since Underworld

00:02:21.359 --> 00:02:25.489
— and a good example of his better work
is the live-action Swamp Thing series.

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:29.500
He served as a director for the first two
episodes as well as an executive producer

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.260
on the series, so it's entirely possible that
he could bring some interesting flair to Ballerina.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.100
Regardless of how you feel about Wiseman's
involvement, the John Wick series has been

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:42.709
solid so far, so there are many more reasons
to be excited about Ballerina than there are

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:43.709
to worry.

00:02:43.709 --> 00:02:48.049
First and foremost, Ana de Armas has firmly
established herself as one of the most exciting

00:02:48.049 --> 00:02:52.360
actresses working today, and fans have come
out in full support of her casting.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.409
As one Redditor says:

00:02:53.409 --> 00:02:55.489
"I would watch this woman do her taxes."

00:02:55.489 --> 00:02:58.660
But it's not just Redditors showing some love
toward de Armas.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.010
On Twitter, one user wrote:

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:03.379
"Ana De Armas is starring in the John Wick
spin-off Ballerina.

00:03:03.379 --> 00:03:05.709
That's all the information that I need about
the project.

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:06.709
I'm sold."

00:03:06.709 --> 00:03:09.690
"It's like destiny that we were meant to meet."

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:13.819
No doubt part of that excitement came from
the actress' role in No Time to Die, in which

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:16.450
she played a gun-toting CIA agent.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:20.650
Many people seem to see her casting as an
extension of that action-packed role; one,

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:21.730
for example, Tweeted:

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:25.490
"Hollywood: Remember the fun part of that
James Bond movie... alright how about we do

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:27.060
a whole movie about that."

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.830
It's important to note that, since it hasn't
even begun filming, we're not going to see

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:32.409
a Ballerina trailer for some time.

00:03:32.409 --> 00:03:36.651
Clearly, there's still a lot left to be revealed
about this latest project, and for now, it

00:03:36.651 --> 00:03:38.579
might just be best to keep an open mind.

00:03:38.579 --> 00:03:43.090
After all, if any franchise can pull off a
pleasant surprise, it's John Wick.

